    "description": {
      "value": "\n<p><strong>Circuitborn Line.</strong> The salvage-recursive. Built from the parts of older Circuitborn that didn’t make it. You carry their last instructions in your firmware.</p><p><em>“Nothing in this world is wasted. Some of it is just waiting to be re-purposed.”</em></p><p><strong>Salvage.</strong> You are a sentient chassis built around the principle of <em>recovery</em>. Broken things speak to you. So do broken people, when they don’t know they’re doing it.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid (Construct-Living).</li><li><strong>Chassis Lean.</strong> Your chassis is built around <strong>BOD (Body)</strong>—expressed primarily through Tier powers.</li><li><strong>Scrap Memory.</strong> You can identify the original purpose of any handheld broken object you touch (1/Soma Break, GM adjudicates depth of detail).</li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
